pend...@hotmail.com wrote:

> What would be a good quest artifact?

> Something that would be useful, Narnia-themed, and
> be a help without breaking the game?

The obvious candidate is "the wardrobe", but what
should it do?

1) I'd suggest it be a speed "slow" form of
Twoflower's "Luggage", an infinite capacity storage
that follows the PC, somewhat like a pet but not
with leashing or magic whistle summoning, and only
able to hold things that get _worn_, as a wardrobe
should do. That would be: armor, lenses, blindfolds,
rings, towels; anything else?

Since spare armor isn't stuff one normally carts
around, but a good selection of boots and robes
might be nice, and backups for stuff getting
disenchanted might also be handy, and the rest are
trivial to carry anyway, this would just decrease
burden a bit compared to normal play, thus maybe not
being too overpowered.

2) Another choice, as in the stories, would be that
the wardrobe act as a portal of some sort. Having it
act as a/the only portal to an entire Narnia themed
dungeon branch _other than_ the quest, and having it
be wishable by other classes, would make it quite
desirable among artifacts.

Maybe even make it be both, since the first one is a
bit wimpy.

Were you planning a new class, perhaps "human
child" (a non-combat class?), to go with this?

FWIW.

